# Files Fern must not modify or delete when regenerating this repo.
#
# Fern owns the SDK source and the ci.yml beside this workflow, and prunes anything it
# did not generate — it reads this file from the pull request's base branch, so an entry
# only protects a file once it is on main.
#
# publish-main.yml is hand-written. Go has no registry: distribution is this repository,
# served to consumers through proxy.golang.org, so "publishing" is pushing a vX.Y.Z tag.
# The workflow releases whopsdk-go when a merge to main lands a core/request_option.go
# whose X-Fern-SDK-Version stamp is not yet tagged. It needs no credential beyond the
# GITHUB_TOKEN that pushes the tag.
#
# Two consequences of that shape are irreversible and worth stating here:
#
#   * proxy.golang.org caches a version permanently and immutably. Once it has served
#     github.com/whopio/whopsdk-go@vX.Y.Z, moving the tag changes nothing for anyone who
#     already fetched it, and the mistake is invisible locally. The workflow refuses to
#     move an existing tag and refuses to release a version the proxy already serves.
#
#   * The module path in go.mod is the import path. It must equal the repository URL, and
#     from v2 onwards it must carry a /vN suffix or every consumer breaks. The workflow
#     checks both against the version it is about to tag.
#
# The Fern Go generator's ci.yml only compiles, lints and tests. Unlike the Ruby
# generator's, it contains no tag-triggered publish job and no id-token: write, so it is
# left to Fern rather than being taken over here.
#
# LICENSE is listed pre-emptively: Fern does not carry one over, and a public Go module
# without one is not safely consumable.
.github/workflows/publish-main.yml
LICENSE
